@startuml button

title User Button Debouncing

' UML 2.5.1: every branch of a fork either joins or ends. The ISR branch and
' the task branch both run forever, so each one ends with "detach" instead of
' flowing into an unreachable final node.

note right
    Design: the ISR only reports that a button edge was detected.
    Every edge restarts the debounce timer of that button. The task
    evaluates the pin level once the timer expired, which means the
    level was stable for DEBOUNCING_TIME (100 ms).
end note

start

:Install the ISR on falling and rising edge
for every button;

fork

    :Send the button id to the queue;

    note right: Runs in the ISR.

    detach

fork again

    repeat

        :Wait up to DEBOUNCING_TIME / 4 (25 ms)
        for a button id on the queue;

        if (Button id received?) then (yes)
            :(Re)start the debounce timer
            (DEBOUNCING_TIME) of that button;
        else (no)
        endif

        while (For every button?) is (next button)

            if (Debounce timer running and timed out?) then (yes)

                :Read the button pin level;
                :Derive PRESSED or RELEASED from the level;

                if (State differs from the stored one?) then (yes)
                    :Store the new button state;
                    :Notify the observer;
                else (no)
                endif

                :Stop the debounce timer;

            else (no)
            endif

        endwhile (all buttons done)

    repeat while (Run forever?) is (yes)

    detach

end fork

@enduml
